.TH MC1-SLURM-DEPLOY 1 "2026-10-08" "mu2edaq-batch-queues" "Mu2e DAQ Tools"
.SH NAME
mc1-slurm-deploy \- install, check and validate Slurm on the Mu2e MC1 trigger cluster
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mc1-slurm-deploy
.RB { preflight | deploy | storage | accounts | firewall | nfs | cvmfs | validate }
.RB [ \-\-apply ]
.RB [ \-\-limit
.IR pattern ]
.RB [ \-\-tags
.IR tags ]
.RB [ \-\-jump
.IR user@host ]
.RB [ \-\-ssh\-user
.IR user ]
.RB [ \-\-puppet\-policy
.RB { fail | warn }]
.RB [ \-\-set
.IR key=value ]...
.RB [ \-\-env\-file
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-print ]
.RB [ \-v ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mc1-slurm-deploy
runs this repository's Ansible playbooks against the hosts in
.IR config/inventory.yml .
Every connection goes through the ProxyJump hop
.RB ( mu2eshift@g2gateway01.fnal.gov
by default) and logs in to the workers as
.BR root .
.TP
.B preflight
Read-only. Checks the OS, short hostname, cgroup v2, chrony offset, Puppet
agent state, the configured UIDs and GIDs, the presence of the job accounts,
the Slurm version the repositories offer, and compute-to-controller
reachability. It also prints each node's CPU and memory layout.
.TP
.B deploy
Runs preflight, then creates the accounts and installs MUNGE (one key,
generated on the controller), Slurm, MariaDB and slurmdbd, and the firewalld
rules. It starts slurmctld on the controller and slurmd on the compute nodes,
and registers the job users with slurmdbd. Without
.B \-\-apply
it runs with
.B \-\-check \-\-diff
and changes nothing. On nodes where Slurm is not yet installed, the dry run
cannot show steps that depend on files the packages would create; those tasks
are reported as ignored errors.
.TP
.B storage
Only the
.I /scratch
and
.I /data-local
logical volumes (and
.IR /nfshome ,
.I /nfsdata
on workers 17 and 18).
.TP
.B accounts
Only the service and job accounts, their
.I .k5login
files and the job accounts' login environment.
.TP
.B firewall
Only the cluster firewalld zone and its guard,
.BR mc1-fw-zone-guard (8).
.TP
.B nfs
NFS exports from workers 17 and 18 and automounts on every worker. Inert
unless
.B mc1_nfs_enabled
is true; refuses while the SLAM Puppet catalog pins nfs-server to stopped.
.TP
.B cvmfs
Installs the CernVM-FS client from the bundle made by
.BR mc1-cvmfs-fetch-rpms (1),
writes
.IR /etc/cvmfs/default.local ,
and mounts each repository in
.B mc1_cvmfs_repositories
at
.I /cvmfs/<repo>
from
.I /etc/fstab
(no autofs). Before any change it refuses if the Puppet catalog manages
CVMFS, if autofs owns
.IR /cvmfs ,
or if the cache filesystem cannot hold
.BR mc1_cvmfs_quota_mb ;
it also reports whether the WPAD (or the configured proxy) and a stratum 1
answer, and stops if neither does. Inert unless
.B mc1_cvmfs_enabled
is true; it is false because the site already installs CVMFS on the MC1
workers, and the role must not overwrite that configuration.
.PP
Every action except
.B preflight
and
.B validate
runs with
.B \-\-check \-\-diff
unless
.B \-\-apply
is given.
.TP
.B validate
Runs test jobs as the first new job account: scontrol ping, node state,
a MUNGE round trip, srun and sbatch on every compute node, cgroup memory
enforcement, a multi-node step, a listing of every CVMFS repository from a job
on each compute node, and sacct records. It writes
.IR results/validate-<UTC>.json .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-apply
deploy only: make changes.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " pattern"
Restrict the run to an Ansible host pattern, e.g.
.BR slurm_compute .
Firewall sources are computed from the facts of all cluster nodes, so a
limited deploy should set
.B mc1_cluster_addrs
explicitly.
.TP
.BI \-\-tags " tags"
Run only tasks with these Ansible tags.
.TP
.BI \-\-jump " user@host"
ProxyJump hop (variable
.BR mc1_jump ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-user " user"
Login on the workers (variable
.BR mc1_ssh_user ).
.TP
.BR \-\-puppet\-policy " " fail | warn
What preflight does when puppet.service is running (variable
.BR mc1_puppet_policy ).
.TP
.BI \-\-set " key=value"
Override any variable in
.IR config/group_vars/all.yml .
Values are typed as YAML. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " path"
dotenv file read below the environment (default
.IR .env
in the repository root).
.TP
.B \-\-print
Print the ansible-playbook command and the merged overrides; run nothing.
.TP
.B \-v
Pass verbosity to ansible-playbook; repeat up to four times.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Precedence, highest first: command line, environment, .env,
.IR config/group_vars/all.yml .
The overrides are handed to Ansible as extra variables.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MC1_JUMP
ProxyJump hop.
.TP
.B MC1_SSH_USER
Login on the workers.
.TP
.B MC1_PUPPET_POLICY
fail or warn.
.TP
.B MC1_SET
Semicolon-separated
.I key=value
overrides, e.g.
.BR "MC1_SET='slurm_debug=debug;slurm_def_mem_per_cpu=4000'" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/inventory.yml
Controller and compute node groups.
.TP
.I config/group_vars/all.yml
All settings: accounts and UIDs, ports, partitions, FUTURE nodes, slurmdbd.
.TP
.I results/
Validation output (git-ignored).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
klist
\&./bootstrap.sh
scripts/mc1-slurm-deploy preflight
scripts/mc1-slurm-deploy deploy                     # dry run with diffs
scripts/mc1-slurm-deploy deploy \-\-apply
scripts/mc1-slurm-deploy validate
scripts/mc1-slurm-deploy deploy \-\-set mc1_job_accounts=... \-\-print
.fi
.SH NOTES
Secrets never leave the cluster. The MUNGE key is generated on the controller
and copied to the compute nodes inside the Ansible run (base64 over the
existing ssh channel, not logged). The slurmdbd database password is generated
in
.I /etc/slurm/.slurmdbd-db.pw
on the controller.
.PP
Claude Code's auto-mode classifier treats these logins as production access.
Run the tool from your own shell, or with the
.B !
prefix inside a session.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of ansible-playbook. 1 if it is not installed; 2 for a
malformed
.BR \-\-set .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mc1-slurm-presurvey (1),
.BR ansible-playbook (1),
.BR slurm.conf (5),
.BR slurmdbd.conf (5),
.BR cgroup.conf (5),
.BR munge (7)
